schema: spec-driven

context: |
  Language: {{ work_language }}
  All artifacts must be written in {{ 'Japanese' if work_language == 'ja' else 'English' }}.
  Keep OpenSpec structural headings and SHALL/MUST keywords in English.

rules:
  design:
    - 'Write only the decisions the implementation needs. An agreement already made is referenced in one line with its source, not copied.'
    - 'Write each decision under a heading `### D<n> <title>` (D1, D2, ...), so tasks can refer to it by number.'
    - 'Include a test plan table: each behavior (each delta-spec scenario) and the one layer that tests it. Defaults are in docs/harness/testing.md: E2E only for one happy path per feature across API, UI and DB; UI detail in component tests; visual detail in style lint or visual tests only. A second layer for the same behavior needs a reason in the table.'
    - 'Write each ruling as `Ruling / Reason / Cost if wrong`, under a heading with the date and a title. Rulings live only here; the Issue links them.'
    - 'Keep the change within budget: at most 15 tasks and 30,000 characters across tasks.md and design.md together. Over budget, split it into independently shippable changes.'
  tasks:
    - 'tasks.md is also the implementation plan. Do not write a separate design or plan document outside the change directory.'
    - 'tasks.md holds the plan only. Execution records (review verdicts, carry-overs, mutation-check results) go to the ledger, rulings to design.md, Minor findings stay in the review reports.'
    - 'Write `Issue: #<n>` on the first line once the Issue exists.'
    - 'Write each task as `- [ ] N.M <what to do>` and indent these labels below it. The labels may be translated into the artifact language; keep the order and the meaning.'
    - '`Refs:` mandatory. The Requirement names (from the delta specs) and the design.md decisions (`D<n>`) the task implements. The implementer and the task or batch reviewer read only the task, what its `Refs:` names and the `Interface:` it uses, so name everything the task needs.'
    - 'design.md heads each decision `### D<n> <title>` so that `Refs:` can name it.'
    - '`Files:` the files to create, change and test.'
    - '`Interface:` names and types that other tasks use. Omit it when no other task uses any.'
    - '`Test first:` for a code task, the test file that goes red first and what it checks. For a task that changes no code, `Verify:` the command and the expected result instead.'
    - '`Review:` `solo` or `batch <letter>`. Solo only for the risk marks `security`, `authz`, `data` and `migration`; every other task, `ui` included, is batched four to six at a time (the remainder may form a smaller batch). A change of three tasks or fewer may write `final` on every task, risk marks included: no intermediate review, only the final review.'
    - '`Risk:` marks such as `security`, `authz`, `data`, `migration`, `ui`, or any the project adds. `ui` marks a batch, not a solo review. Use `none` when there is no mark.'
    - 'Write no code snippets. The implementer writes the code.'
    - 'Map each delta-spec scenario to the task that verifies it, in a short list. A scenario with no test and no verify step is a defect in the plan.'
